{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqvlebvwttg","workspace":"D:\\PersonalProject\\zonoid","title":"Headless claude print mode duplicate tool use id 400 fixed by CLI upgrade to 2.1.195","summary":"CONFIRMED FIX of the prior finding: the HTTP 400 \"messages.1.content.N: `tool_use` ids must be unique\" on headless `claude -p` was a Claude Code CLI 2.1.1 harness bug (mis-assembled the first assistant message with duplicate tool_use ids on the wire). Upgrading the CLI to 2.1.195 fully resolves it — verified two ways: (1) a standalone multi-tool prompt (ls + read README) now completes cleanly with no duplicate-id error; (2) the ARC-AGI-3 Mode 0 bench A/B (runner.py --agent-command \"claude -p\") now runs both arms to exit_code 0 with coherent agent output and a rendered report, where before both arms exited 1 with the 400. Install note for this box: the active CLI is the NATIVE install at C:/Users/yuepr/.local/bin/claude (NOT npm global); update it with `claude install` (after `npm -g uninstall @anthropic-ai/claude-code` to clear the leftover npm copy), not `npm i -g`. Reproduced independently of zonoid/MCP, so this was never a zonoid bug. Remaining bench 0% pass is expected, not a bug: arc-agi-3-smoke-1 is a placeholder with no real grid, and bare `claude -p` gates tool calls behind permission prompts (auto-denied headless) plus the context JSON sits outside the allowed working dirs — so the agent correctly refuses rather than fabricating. A real agentic Mode 0 run needs permission/allowedTools flags + an in-workspace context file + a real ARC task id.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-26T23:59:02.828Z","vec":[-0.10043329745531082,0.01266495417803526,-0.08024196326732635,0.0068040648475289345,0.02716337889432907,-0.08020922541618347,-0.004090726841241121,0.009258603677153587,-0.02122005820274353,-0.0010358694707974792,0.05647767335176468,-0.03583596274256706,0.07728035748004913,-0.02442585676908493,0.0022583119571208954,0.0296880137175321